  "flags": {
    "seattle-by-night": {
      "origen": "escena",
      "escena": "torre-boveda",
      "id": "LUG-06",
      "plano": "torre-boveda",
      "provisional": false,
      "nota": "<p><strong>Location:</strong> @UUID[JournalEntry.L6Fl1S0tjkWno2we]{Halloway Tower}<br><strong>Scenes:</strong> @UUID[JournalEntry.doItxeK8y7M1PufU.JournalEntryPage.snrsN5RkdAklRIDn]{A4-E01 · Primogen Council}</p>\n<p><strong>The vault on level −3</strong>, “accessible only by the private elevator” (LUG-06). The car opens onto a concrete antechamber with a single steel door, locked with a combination (Mr. Pell knows it; with 3 or more successes on the ferry, A4-E03, he hands it over along with the elevator key). In the car, the door half receives arrivals and the back half goes up to the penthouse (plan “torre-atico”).</p>\n<p><strong>What it holds</strong> (LUG-06): the <strong>original of Vance&#39;s journals</strong> (bought in 1986), <strong>copy 1 of 3</strong>, typewritten by Pell, and, since Night 6, the <strong>original drive of the File</strong> (and USB drive 3 if Lonnie died that night). The journals and the copy on the shelves; the drive in the safe. On the night of the Council, the <strong>aluminum briefcase</strong> waits on the steel table.</p>\n<p><strong>A4-E01 → A4-E03.</strong> If Halloway flees, “he takes the private elevator down to level −3, takes the briefcase out of the vault, and hands it to Pell.” An infiltration before the climax also ends here, if the coterie plans one.</p>\n\n<p class=\"sbn-moviles\">The movable furniture (1) are unlocked tiles: they can be moved, knocked over or used as a barricade.</p>",
      "moviles": []
    }
